course: dictionary
lesson: 13908
title: Latino: family and culture
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Latino is a word about where a family comes from. In the USA, a Latino is a person whose family comes from Latin America, such as Mexico, Puerto Rico, Cuba or Colombia. «My friend Sofia is Latino; her family comes from Mexico.» The clue is in the rest of the sentence: her family comes from Mexico.
explain: Latino can also describe things, like music, food and culture. «We ate tamales at a Latino family party.» Here Latino tells you what kind of party it was: one with food and customs from Latin America.
explain: People choose different words for themselves. «Latina» is used for women, and «Latinx» or «Latine» are used for everyone. «Hispanic» is used for Spanish-speaking heritage. If you are not sure what someone prefers, ask them politely.
fact: Latino means a person in the USA whose family comes from Latin America.
fact: As an adjective, Latino describes things, such as Latino music, Latino food or Latino culture.
fact: «Latina» is used for women.
fact: «Latinx» and «Latine» are used for everyone, and «Hispanic» is used for Spanish-speaking heritage.
fact: Hispanic Heritage Month is a time in the USA when people celebrate the history and culture of Latino and Hispanic families.
exercise: «My friend Sofia is Latino; her family comes from Mexico.» What does Latino mean here? | A person who lives on a farm | A person who speaks only English | A kind of school bus | *A person whose family comes from Latin America
exercise: «We ate tamales at a Latino family party.» In this sentence, what does Latino describe? | The time the party started | *The family's Latin American food and customs | The weather that day | The number of guests
exercise: Which word is used for a woman whose family comes from Latin America? | Hispanic | Latino | *Latina | Latinx
test: Which word is the adjective in «We love Latino music»? | We | music | love | *Latino
test: Which word can be used for everyone, not just for women? | Latina | *Latine | Latinas | Latinos only
exam: Which is the best meaning of Latino? | *A person in the USA whose family comes from Latin America | A type of music from Japan | A town in Mexico | A person in the USA whose family comes from Canada
